        },
        {
          "id": 493501940,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The partial reversion also slows down startup as described in #15296. Prior to this being merged, ctest took about 3 minutes on the Windows builders. It now takes 8 to 9 minutes.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-25T17:55:20.850Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-25T17:55:20.850Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 85721397,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1774,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 493557691,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Should it be reverted and replaced by a more targeted fix?\n\nWhat sort of targeted fix, that will ensure that, if there are any extcap preferences set in the preferences file, the extcap preferences will have been loaded before the preferences file is read, are you considering?\n\nWould keeping a cache of extcap information, so that information that changes only if the set of extcaps changes is only fetched the first time SomethingShark is started and times when SomethingShark detects that an extcap has been added, removed, or changed, handle this?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-25T18:53:06.613Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-25T18:53:06.613Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 85721397,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1774,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 493780398,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Or 2) treat preferences beginning with \"extcap.\" specially:\n\n- when reading the preferences, don't print a warning if the preference doesn't exist, just stash the string value in a list of \"deferred extcap preference settings\";\n- the first time extcap information is needed for any reason, call `extcap_register_preferences()` and then do a \"deferred registration\" of the stashed preferences (reporting any errors at that point).",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-26T03:14:53.309Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-26T03:14:53.309Z",
