          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 496688703,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`ui/qt/main.cpp` calls `commandline_early_options()`, which gets things in order prior to calling `epan_init()`. Would it make sense do do something similar in `tshark.c`, e.g. call `capture_early_options()`, which would look for:\n\n- -G {defaultprefs,currentprefs}\n- -i\n- -o extcap:...\n\nand call `extcap_register_preferences()` if any are present?",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
